.TH GAIKSAURUS 1 "October 2026" "" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gaiksaurus \- graphical English thesaurus (GTK+ front end for Aiksaurus)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gaiksaurus
[\fB\-t\fR [\fB\-m\fR]]
[\fIword\fR]
.br
.B gaiksaurus
.RB { \-h | \-\-help | \-v | \-\-version }
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gaiksaurus
is a graphical interface to the Aiksaurus English thesaurus library.
Type a word into the
.B Look up
box and press Enter (or click the search button) to see its synonyms,
grouped by meaning.
Click a word in the results to select it, and double-click it to look it up.
The back and forward buttons, and the menus next to them, move through the
list of words looked up earlier.
.PP
If a
.I word
is given on the command line, it is looked up immediately.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-tray
Also show an icon in the system tray (notification area).
The thesaurus window opens as usual.
Clicking the tray icon shows the window, or hides it if it is already
visible.
Closing the window only hides it; the program keeps running in the tray.
The right-click menu of the icon has
.B Show/Hide
and
.B Quit
entries.
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-minimized
Only meaningful together with
.BR \-\-tray .
Start hidden in the tray instead of opening the window.
If a
.I word
is given on the command line the window is opened anyway.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a short help message and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print version and license information and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B gaiksaurus happy
Look up "happy" in the thesaurus window.
.TP
.B gaiksaurus \-\-tray
Open the window and keep an icon in the system tray.
.TP
.B gaiksaurus \-\-tray \-\-minimized
Start hidden in the system tray; click the icon to open the thesaurus.
This is a good command for a session autostart entry.
.SH NOTES
The tray icon uses the GtkStatusIcon interface.
It needs a desktop that provides a system tray (for example Xfce, or KDE
with its legacy tray support); on desktops without one the program still
works, but without a tray icon.
.PP
The icon is installed in the hicolor icon theme as
.IR gaiksaurus .
The thesaurus data files are installed in
.IR /usr/share/aiksaurus/ .
.SH SEE ALSO
.UR http://www.aiksaurus.com/
Aiksaurus home page
.UE
